  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Creditel - Green Hydrogen</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project contributes to Uruguays efforts to reduce the carbon footprint of hard-to-abate sectors (such as transport, industrial heating, steel production, and oil refining). Furthermore, at the market level, the Project and the Sub-project are expected align with the sustainability agenda of the Government of Uruguay, which envisions in its GH Roadmap an increase in the participation of FCEVs in the local fleet of heavy trucks.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed investment consists of a senior A loan of up to US$ 20 million to Socur S.A. (Creditel or the Company) to finance the development of a green hydrogen (GH) plant in Uruguay (the Project). Creditel will own the project assets, which in turn will be operated by and leased to Kahir&#xf3;s, a special purpose vehicle (the Sub-project). The A Loan will have 7-year tenor, which IFC will help structure as a green loan.</narrative>
  </description>
